  "liner": {
   "body_md": "Mountain Goats performed a full-length set at the City Winery on Monday, April 11, 2016, as the first of three consecutive nights at that venue [1]. This specific recording, titled tMG2016-14-11, captures the entire twenty-one song performance, which lasted approximately ninety-eight minutes [1]. The uploader noted that they only recorded this first show of the three-night run [1]. The setlist includes a mix of well-known tracks and deeper cuts, such as \"Get Lonely,\" \"Until I Am Whole,\" and \"Damn These Vampires\" [1]. Notably, the band played \"Maize Stalk Drinking Blood,\" a rare track with only thirteen archived performances, and \"Rotten Stinking Mouthpiece,\" which has eight archived performances [2]. The show also featured \"Soft Targets,\" a bustout that had not been played in one hundred and four archived shows or 3,082 days, and \"Enoch 18:14,\" a bustout absent for 1,032 days [2]. Other songs included \"Stabbed to Death Outside San Juan,\" \"Never Quite Free,\" \"Romans 10:9,\" \"Deuteronomy 2:10,\" and \"Southwestern Territory\" [1]. The latter part of the set featured \"Woke Up New,\" \"New Monster Avenue,\" \"Alpha Rats Nest,\" \"The Young Thousands,\" and \"Liza Forever Minnelli\" [1]. The performance concluded with \"Up the Wolves,\" \"Love Love Love,\" \"No Children,\" and \"Spent Gladiator 2\" [1]. This is the 219th show in the archive's collection for the band, following a previous archived performance at Asbury Hall on April 6, 2016 [2]. As the only available recording of this specific date, it offers a complete view of that particular night's musical flow [1].",
